 eye of everyman: witnessing DNA in the Simpson trial</article-title><source>Social Stud Sci</source><volume>28</volume><issue>5&#x02013;6</issue><fpage>713</fpage><lpage>740</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b24-ehp0116-000123"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jasanoff</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Weil</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Hidden experts: judging science after <italic>Daubert</italic></article-title><source>Trying Times: Science and Responsibilities after <italic>Daubert</italic></source><publisher-loc>Chicago</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Illinois Institute of Technology</publisher-name><fpage>30</fpage><lpage>47</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b25-ehp0116-000123"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jasanoff</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Law&#x02019;s knowledge: science for justice in legal settings</article-title><source>Am J Public Health</source><volume>95</volume><issue>S11</issue><fpage>S49</fpage><lpage>S58</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16030338</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b26-ehp0116-000123"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krimsky</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><source>Science in the Private Interest: How the Lure of Profits Has Corrupted the Virtue of Biomedical Research</source><publisher-loc>Lanham, MD</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Rowman &#x00026; Littlefield</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b27-ehp0116-000123"><note><p><italic>Kumho Tire Co. v. Carmichael</italic>. 1999. 526 U.S. 137, U.S. Supreme Court.</p></note></ref><ref id="b28-ehp0116-000123"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="aut